(14796, 62, 93, 1871, 8, '2026-04-27 11:00:00', '2026-04-27 12:00:00', NULL, NULL, NULL, 60, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 'NOTELAB ANALYSIS\nEMANUELA PANATTA\nClass: GESE 5\n\nTest 1\nGeneral Summary\nKeycode:79917050\nStatus:Completed\nSuccessfully used:\nMedal\nFunctions\nGrade 3\n\nMedal\nGrammar\nGrade 4\n\nMedal\nVocabulary\nGrade 2\n\nIn Task 1, the student answered most questions, but several responses were incomplete, unclear, or did not fully address what was asked. In Task 2, most answers were related to the questions, but some were only partly relevant or off-target.\n\nThe student successfully used Functions, Grammar, and Vocabulary topics that are assessed in GESE Grade 2 (A1). They also attempted points from Grade 3 (A2.1), Grade 4 (A2.2), and Grade 5 (B1).\n\nSpecific recommendations on Functions, Grammar points, and Vocabulary for the student to practice are listed below.\n\nTask Fulfillment\nTask 1: Describing a picture of a family\nDescriptor\nFullness of response: How complete and detailed the answer is.\nStudent performance\nThe student partially answers by mentioning some elements of the picture like the family, children, and animals.\nPartial\nDescriptor\nRelevance of response: How relevant the information in the answer is to the question.\nStudent performance\nThe information is partly relevant but lacks detail about many elements in the picture.\nPartial\nTask 2: Having a conversation about daily routines, holidays, and pets\nDescriptor\nFullness of response: How complete and detailed the answer is.\nStudent performance\nThe student answers most questions, but several responses are incomplete, unclear, or do not fully address what was asked.\nPartial\nDescriptor\nRelevance of response: How relevant the information in the answer is to the question.\nStudent performance\nMost answers are related to the questions, but some are only partly relevant or off-target, such as responses about pets\' age and where they sleep.\nPartial\nLanguage Functions\nEMANUELA successfully used functions from:\nMedal\nIdentifying and naming items: Immediate surroundings including classroom objects, Basic parts of the face and body, Common animals, Cardinal numbers up to 20, Colours, Everyday items of clothing\nGrade 1\n\nMedal\nDescribing people, animals, objects and places very simply\nGrade 2\n\nMedal\nStating simple facts\nGrade 2\n\nEMANUELA may need to practise:\nIndicating the position of people and objects\nInforming about possessions\nMore details\nGrammar\nEMANUELA successfully used functions from:\nMedal\nThe present simple tense of the verb \'to be\'\nGrade 1\n\nMedal\nSimple adjectives, eg \'small\', \'tall\', \'green\'\nGrade 1\n\nMedal\nPresent simple tense\nGrade 2\n\nEMANUELA may need to practise:\n\'has/have got\' / \'have you got?\' / \'Do you have?\'\nDeterminers \'their\', \'its\'\nPossessive pronouns \'mine\', \'yours\', \'his\', \'hers\'\nMore details\nVocabulary\nEMANUELA used appropriate vocabulary for topics that are covered in:\nMedal\nImmediate surroundings including classroom objects\nGrade 1\n\nMedal\nCardinal numbers up to 20\nGrade 1\n\nMedal\nColours\nGrade 1\n\nEMANUELA may need to practise:\nEveryday items of clothing', 'IN-CLASS: HW checked, we did diagnostic tool test on notelab - it went quite well + speaking practise', '2026-04-27 07:08:23', 13, 1, 0, 'Inglese', '2026-03-31 10:21:26', '2026-04-27 09:02:45'),
